course: dictionary
lesson: 6536
title: Neutral: not taking sides
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Neutral» means not taking any side. A neutral referee blows the whistle fairly and does not cheer for either team. A neutral place is one that belongs to neither person, so nobody has an advantage there.
explain: «A handover is when one parent brings the child to the other; meeting in a neutral place like a car park keeps it calm and quick.» The car park is a neutral place because it is not either parent's home. Neither side has the advantage, so the handover stays calm.
explain: Neutral can also mean having no strong feeling or no bright colour. «Neutral colours» are beige, grey or cream. A «neutral face» shows no strong feeling. In science, a neutral substance is neither acid nor alkali, like pure water.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The King stays neutral and does not vote.» If you put in «does not take sides», the sentence still makes sense, so neutral means not taking sides here.
fact: Neutral means not taking any side in an argument, game or war.
fact: On the pH scale, 7 is neutral, like pure water. Below 7 is acid, and above 7 is alkali.
fact: A neutral country stays out of a war.
fact: Neutral colours are not bright. They are beige, grey or cream.
fact: Neutral is an adjective, but it can also be a noun: in a car, neutral is the gear where the engine is not connected to the wheels.
exercise: «A handover is when one parent brings the child to the other; meeting in a neutral place like a car park keeps it calm and quick.» What does neutral place mean here? | A place full of loud music | A place painted grey | *A place that belongs to neither parent | A place with the most shops
exercise: «Scientists measure acids and alkalis on the pH scale from 0 to 14: below 7 is acid, 7 is neutral like pure water, above 7 is alkali.» What pH number is neutral? | 0 | 3 | 14 | *7
exercise: «Red cabbage juice is purple in neutral water, pink-red with acid, blue-green with a mild alkali like baking soda, and yellow with a very strong alkali.» What colour is the juice in neutral water? | blue-green | pink-red | *purple | yellow
test: «Mayors, governors and premiers are chosen in elections or by elected bodies, but the King is not elected; he stays neutral and does not vote.» What does stays neutral mean for the King? | He paints the palace grey | *He does not take a side | He votes for the winner | He is chosen by the children
test: Which of these is a neutral colour? | Neon green | *Beige | Hot pink | Bright red
exam: The referee stayed neutral during the match. What does this mean? | He cheered loudly for the home team | He ran faster than all the players | *He took no side between the teams | He wore a bright red shirt
